{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"title","type":"text","text":"# LLM Knowledge Base — System Architecture\nHow raw sources flow through the LLM pipeline into a structured, queryable wiki.\nBuilt with Claude as the LLM engine and Obsidian as the viewing frontend.","x":-300,"y":-700,"width":600,"height":120,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"raw-dir","type":"text","text":"# raw/\n**Raw Source Ingestion**\n\nUnprocessed inputs: PDFs, articles, transcripts, Twitter threads, HN discussions, research papers.\n\nThese are the ground-truth documents — never modified by the LLM.\n\n- 9+ raw files currently\n- Formats: .txt, .md, .pdf\n- Added manually by the human curator","x":-1400,"y":-400,"width":450,"height":300,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"claude-md","type":"text","text":"# CLAUDE.md\n**System Instructions**\n\nThe master prompt file that defines:\n- Wiki structure and conventions\n- Article templates\n- Linking rules\n- Quality standards\n- Tool usage protocols\n\nThis is the \"constitution\" of the KB system.","x":-300,"y":-400,"width":450,"height":300,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"claude-md-file","type":"file","file":"CLAUDE.md","x":-300,"y":-50,"width":450,"height":200,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"wiki-dir","type":"text","text":"# wiki/\n**Compiled Wiki Output**\n\nLLM-authored structured knowledge:\n\n- **_index.md** — Master index of all articles\n- **_meta/** — summaries.md, links.md\n- **concepts/** — 20 concept articles\n- **sources/** — 40+ source summaries\n- **entities/** — 23 entity profiles\n\nAll content authored by Claude, cross-linked via wikilinks.","x":500,"y":-400,"width":500,"height":340,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"wiki-index","type":"file","file":"wiki/_index.md","x":1100,"y":-400,"width":400,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"wiki-summaries","type":"file","file":"wiki/_meta/summaries.md","x":1100,"y":-170,"width":400,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"wiki-links","type":"file","file":"wiki/_meta/links.md","x":1100,"y":60,"width":400,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"wiki-concepts","type":"text","text":"# wiki/concepts/\n20 concept articles covering:\n- Core system (LLM-KB, compilation, QA)\n- Retrieval (RAG vs index, vector DBs)\n- Quality (hallucination, data quality)\n- Knowledge rep (graphs, agents)\n- Human workflow (PKM, second brain)","x":1100,"y":290,"width":400,"height":220,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"wiki-sources","type":"text","text":"# wiki/sources/\n40+ source summaries including:\n- Karpathy's original thread\n- DAIR.AI, Glen Rhodes analyses\n- KARMA, STORM papers\n- Embedding/RAG technique sources\n- Vector DB comparisons","x":1100,"y":560,"width":400,"height":200,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"wiki-entities","type":"text","text":"# wiki/entities/\n23 entity profiles:\n- People: Karpathy, Steph Ango, etc.\n- Tools: Obsidian, ChromaDB, FAISS\n- Systems: STORM, KARMA, Graphiti\n- Orgs: DAIR.AI, Zep","x":1100,"y":810,"width":400,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"tools-dir","type":"text","text":"# tools/\n**Automation Scripts**\n\nHelper scripts for the KB pipeline:\n- Ingestion helpers\n- Wiki compilation triggers\n- Health check runners\n- Output generators\n\nThe \"hacky scripts\" Karpathy described — the glue between raw input and wiki output.","x":-1400,"y":200,"width":450,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"output-dir","type":"text","text":"# output/\n**Generated Artifacts**\n\nDerivative products from the compiled wiki:\n- Presentations (Marp slides)\n- Canvas visualizations\n- Exported reports\n- Q&A session logs\n\nProves the KB is a productive asset, not just storage.","x":500,"y":600,"width":450,"height":260,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"templates-dir","type":"text","text":"# templates/\n**Article Templates**\n\nStandardized templates for:\n- Source summaries\n- Concept articles\n- Entity profiles\n\nEnsures consistent structure across all wiki articles.","x":-1400,"y":540,"width":450,"height":220,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"kb-dir","type":"text","text":"# kb/\n**Knowledge Base Config**\n\nConfiguration and metadata for the KB system itself — schemas, settings, and operational parameters.","x":-300,"y":300,"width":450,"height":160,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"obsidian-node","type":"text","text":"# Obsidian (Frontend)\n**Read-Only Viewing IDE**\n\nHumans open the wiki/ folder in Obsidian to:\n- Browse articles via graph view\n- Follow wikilinks between concepts\n- View canvas visualizations\n- Read source summaries\n\nObsidian is the viewer — Claude is the author.","x":500,"y":1000,"width":500,"height":260,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"llm-engine","type":"text","text":"# Claude (LLM Engine)\n**The Author**\n\nClaude performs ALL wiki operations:\n1. **Ingest** — reads raw/ files\n2. **Compile** — writes wiki/ articles\n3. **Query** — answers questions via index\n4. **Maintain** — lints, links, fills gaps\n5. **Generate** — creates output/ artifacts\n\nGoverned by CLAUDE.md instructions.","x":-300,"y":600,"width":500,"height":300,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"phase-ingest","type":"text","text":"## Phase 1: Ingest\nHuman drops files into raw/\nClaude reads and understands them","x":-1400,"y":-650,"width":350,"height":100,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"phase-compile","type":"text","text":"## Phase 2: Compile\nClaude writes source summaries,\nconcept articles, entity profiles,\nupdates _index.md and _meta/","x":200,"y":-650,"width":350,"height":120,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"phase-query","type":"text","text":"## Phase 3: Query\nUser asks questions, Claude\nnavigates index → summaries → articles\nto synthesize answers","x":1200,"y":-650,"width":350,"height":120,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"phase-maintain","type":"text","text":"## Phase 4: Maintain\nClaude runs health checks:\nbroken links, orphans, gaps,\ninconsistencies, new suggestions","x":1600,"y":-400,"width":350,"height":120,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"phase-generate","type":"text","text":"## Phase 5: Generate\nClaude creates derivative\noutputs: slides, canvases,\nreports, exports","x":200,"y":1050,"width":350,"height":100,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"human-node","type":"text","text":"# Human Curator\n- Adds raw sources\n- Asks questions\n- Reviews wiki in Obsidian\n- Directs Claude's work\n- Never edits wiki directly","x":-1400,"y":850,"width":400,"height":200,"color":"1"}
	],
